#: ../../source/user_guide/production_runs.rst:37
msgid "On a SLURM cluster the account, partition, quality of service and GPU request go in the same place. The example below is for Leonardo (Booster partition) at CINECA, where all of them are required; other clusters have their own account, partition and QoS names. For brevity the function below, the same as in the first-run script, applies one set of settings to every calculation; nothing prevents passing different ones per code, which is what `examples/graphene/run_atp.py <https://github.com/aiida-trieste-developers/aiida-trainspot/blob/main/examples/graphene/run_atp.py>`_ does with one block of settings per code. The matching ``computer`` and ``code`` definitions are in `examples/setup_codes <https://github.com/aiida-trieste-developers/aiida-trainspot/tree/main/examples/setup_codes>`_."
msgstr "Suntun cluster SLURM l'account, la partizion, la cualitât dal servizi e la richieste di GPU a van tal stes puest. L'esempli chi sot al è par Leonardo (partizion Booster) al CINECA, dulà che a son ducj obligatoris; altris cluster a àn i lôr nons di account, partizion e QoS. Par brevitât la funzion chi sot, la stesse dal script de prime esecuzion, e aplighe un sôl insiemi di impostazions a ogni calcul; nuie nol impedìs di passâ impostazions diferentis par ogni codiç, che al è ce che al fâs `examples/graphene/run_atp.py <https://github.com/aiida-trieste-developers/aiida-trainspot/blob/main/examples/graphene/run_atp.py>`_ cuntun bloc di impostazions par codiç. Lis definizions di ``computer`` e ``code`` corispondentis a son in `examples/setup_codes <https://github.com/aiida-trieste-developers/aiida-trainspot/tree/main/examples/setup_codes>`_."

#: ../../source/user_guide/production_runs.rst:72
msgid "The attributes set above are standard AiiDA ``CalcJob`` options: ``account``, ``queue_name`` (the SLURM partition), ``qos``, ``custom_scheduler_commands`` (extra lines added to the SLURM script), ``max_wallclock_seconds``, ``max_memory_kb``, ``resources``, ``withmpi``, ``import_sys_environment`` and ``prepend_text``."
msgstr "I atribûts impostâts parsore a son opzions standard dai ``CalcJob`` di AiiDA: ``account``, ``queue_name`` (la partizion SLURM), ``qos``, ``custom_scheduler_commands`` (riis in plui zontadis al script SLURM), ``max_wallclock_seconds``, ``max_memory_kb``, ``resources``, ``withmpi``, ``import_sys_environment`` e ``prepend_text``."

#: ../../source/user_guide/production_runs.rst:80
msgid "Choosing the training engine"
msgstr "Sielzi il motôr di adestrament"

#: ../../source/user_guide/production_runs.rst:82
msgid "The workflow trains its potentials with one of two engines, selected by ``training_engine``: ``\"MACE\"`` (default) or ``\"META\"`` (metatrain). The corresponding AiiDA plugin has to be installed (see :doc:`installation`). The choice matters twice: it decides which inputs are needed for training, and in which format LAMMPS reads the trained potentials, that is, which ``pair_style`` is used in the exploration. The pair style is set with ``exploration.potential_pair_style``, and the LAMMPS executable must have been built with the matching support:"
msgstr "Il flus di lavôr al adestre i siei potenziâi cuntun di doi motôrs, selezionât di ``training_engine``: ``\"MACE\"`` (predefinît) o ``\"META\"`` (metatrain). Il plugin AiiDA corispondent al à di jessi instalât (cjale :doc:`installation`). La sielte e conte dôs voltis: e decît cuai input che a coventin pal adestrament, e in ce formât che LAMMPS al lei i potenziâi adestrâts, ven a stâi cuâl ``pair_style`` che al ven doprât te esplorazion. Il pair style si lu impueste cun ``exploration.potential_pair_style``, e l'eseguibil di LAMMPS al à di jessi stât compilât cul supuart corispondent:"

